course: dictionary
lesson: 16073
title: Wailing: a long, high cry
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wail is a long, loud, high cry. People wail when they are in pain, very sad or angry. «The baby was wailing in the night, and nobody could settle her.» The words in the sentence give the clues: a baby in the night, and nobody could settle her. So wailing means crying loudly for a long time.
explain: Wailing can also describe a sound that is like a cry. «The siren was wailing down the road as the fire engine raced past.» A siren is not crying, but its long, high sound is like a wail. «The wind was wailing in the chimney» means the wind made a long, high, lonely sound. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes wailing is informal, which means it is used in relaxed, everyday speech. «Stop wailing about your homework!» Here wailing means complaining loudly and at length. The sentence does not mean a real cry; it means someone is making a big fuss.
explain: Wailing Wall is a name you may meet. It is an older name for the Western Wall in Jerusalem, a holy place where Jewish people pray. Many people now prefer to say Western Wall. When a word is a name, look for a capital letter and read the words around it.
fact: Wailing means a long, loud, high cry of pain, sadness or anger.
fact: Wailing can describe sounds like a siren or the wind.
fact: Informal wailing means complaining loudly and at length.
fact: «Wailing» can be a noun, a verb (wail, wails, wailed, wailing) or an adjective.
fact: The Wailing Wall is an older name for the Western Wall in Jerusalem, a holy place for Jewish people.
exercise: «The baby was wailing in the night, and nobody could settle her.» What is the baby doing? | *Crying loudly and for a long time | Singing a song | Sleeping quietly | Laughing at a joke
exercise: «The siren was wailing down the road as the fire engine raced past.» What does wailing describe? | A bright light | A strong smell of smoke | A soft touch | *A long, high sound
exercise: «The mourners were wailing at the funeral.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the mourners were doing. | *wailing | were | funeral | mourners
test: Tom says wailing means singing happily. What does wailing mean in «The wind was wailing in the chimney»? | *A long, high, lonely sound | A loud bang | A happy song | A quiet whisper
test: «Stop wailing about your homework!» What does wailing mean here? | *Complaining loudly and at length | Whispering softly | Running fast | Singing loudly
exam: «The Wailing Wall in Jerusalem is also called the Western Wall.» What is the Wailing Wall? | *An older name for the Western Wall, a holy place for Jewish people | A loud siren in Jerusalem | A wall that moves in the wind | A school where children learn to sing
